From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:42:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: send read receipts once a chat is read

No read receipt was ever sent. mark_read_defer() keeps what a receipt
needs - the message id, the chat and the sender - for receipt.c to send
when the conversation is read, but nothing called it: the store stayed
empty, so reading a chat sent nothing, whatever the setting.

Keep each received message in the store, and send them when the chat is
read. The Messaging app reads a chat through the transport, which raises
the "unseen" update Pidgin raises, so make "when interacting with the
conversation" the default (it is the first choice of the option now) in
place of "when sending a reply".

The store is filled on whatsmeow's event goroutine and emptied on
libpurple's main loop, so it is locked now (deferred_receipts.go, with
tests), and a chat's receipts are taken out as they are sent: a receipt
goes once, not again each time the chat is looked at. Sending them is a
round trip to the server per sender, so it no longer runs on the main
loop.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
